  Local operator decision receipt journal
    ✔ anchors batches of ALLOW/BLOCK/ERROR record hashes without changing token balances
    ✔ rejects another writer, duplicate roots, noncontiguous sequences and oversized batches
    ✔ binds leaves to chain, receipt contract, writer, intent, blob and sequence

  CRE authorization and token settlement
    ✔ accepts a workflow report and settles exactly one authorized payment
    ✔ rejects callers other than the trusted forwarder
    ✔ rejects another workflow even through the same forwarder
    ✔ rejects missing workflow metadata
    ✔ rejects cross-chain and cross-contract replay
    ✔ rejects a duplicate request report
    ✔ rejects expired and excessive authorization lifetimes
    ✔ cannot spend a denied report
    ✔ binds authorization to the agent, recipient, token, and amount
    ✔ expires before settlement
    ✔ only allows the configured settlement contract to consume reports
    ✔ rolls authorization back if token transfer fails
    ✔ advertises the CRE receiver and ERC165 interfaces
    ✔ only lets the owner bind or update a deployed workflow ID
    ✔ remains closed when deployed before the workflow ID is available

  AgentPayGuardedStream / local policy authority
    ✔ requires three distinct authorities and a contract token
    ✔ rejects unsigned legacy entry points even with balance and unlimited allowance
    ✔ accepts an exact EIP-712 approval and consumes its nonce with escrow only
    ✔ rejects fabricated, agent-signed, cross-chain and cross-contract approvals
    ✔ binds every signed action field and metadata; caller cannot change the intent
    ✔ rejects expired or overlong approvals, nonce substitution and deposit/rate violations
    ✔ blocks duplicate active funding and session replay after closure
    ✔ does not let the agent or recipient close early without the separate policy signature
    ✔ pays accrued earnings and refunds the remainder exactly once after policy closure
    ✔ allows recipient withdrawals and releases rounding remainder at expiry
    ✔ keeps recovery unavailable to agent/policy keys and works with the signer offline
    ✔ reverts nonce/session consumption when the token deposit fails

  isolated CRE simulation receiver
    ✔ records empty-metadata mock delivery while labeling it as simulation only
    ✔ requires explicit opt-in and a deployed forwarder
    ✔ rejects a direct caller even with empty metadata
    ✔ preserves replay, destination, and expiry bounds
    ✔ cannot be connected to the settlement payment path
    ✔ leaves the strict production consumer closed to missing identity

  AgentPayStream
    Deployment
      ✔ Should set the right tUSD token address
    Stream Creation
      ✔ Should create a stream successfully
      ✔ Should fail if allowance is insufficient
    Withdrawal
      ✔ Should allow withdrawal of accrued tokens
    Cancellation
      ✔ Should allow sender to cancel and refund remaining
    Active Check
      ✔ Should return true for active stream

  Consequential documented payment bounds
    ✔ rejects zero, permits a smaller payment, and consumes all remaining authorization
    ✔ releases division dust after prior withdrawal at expiry; closing then prevents further withdrawal


